>> title: Beef Stroganoff
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: beef, mushrooms, egg noodles, sour cream, one-pot, skillet
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: stroganoff, beef stroganov, bef stroganov, beef and noodles in sour cream
>> servings: 4
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — sour cream splits if it boils, so the pan comes off the heat before it goes in and a split sauce does not come back
>> washing-up: the large skillet, a plate for the seared beef
>> keeps: 2 days — the sour cream splits if you push the heat, and the noodles swell whatever you do

>> step: The noodles cook in the beef's own broth in the same pan. Sear the beef first and it goes back in at the end.
Sear the beef first, take it out to a plate, and it goes back in at the very end.

>> step: sear 3 min, out to a plate
Sear @beef sirloin{1 1/4%lb}(570 g; cut in thin strips), @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} in @unsalted butter{1%Tbs} in a #large skillet{} for ~sear{3%min}, then out to a plate.

>> step: brown 8 min
Brown @cremini mushrooms{12%oz}(340 g; sliced thick), @yellow onion{1%large}(sliced) in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs} for ~brown{8%min}.

>> step: stir in the flour, 1 min
Stir @&(~1)mushrooms{} with @all-purpose flour{2%Tbs}(16 g), @sweet paprika{2%tsp}, @Dijon mustard{1%Tbs} for ~stir{1%min}.

>> step: simmer 12 min, noodles take up the liquid
Simmer @&(~1)pan{} with @beef stock{3%cups}(710 mL), @wide egg noodles{8%oz}(225 g) for ~simmer{12%min}, stirring, until the noodles are tender and the liquid has gone into them.

>> step: fold in off the heat, beef back
Fold @&(~4)seared beef{}, @sour cream{3/4%cup}(180 g), @dill{2%Tbs}(chopped), @black pepper{1/2%tsp} into @&(~1)noodles{} off the heat.

>> step: If the sauce looks tight after the fold, loosen it with a spoonful of hot water and not the burner.
Sour cream splits if it boils, so the pan comes off the heat before it goes in. If the sauce looks tight, loosen it with a spoonful of hot water.
